# Now your most important question

## If ETH becomes quantum-proof, why does QRL need to exist?

This is exactly the right attack on the QRL investment thesis.

And the uncomfortable answer is:

### If Ethereum flawlessly becomes fully quantum-resistant before Q-Day, QRL loses a large part of its easiest narrative advantage.

Very important.

Don't convince yourself otherwise because you own QRL.

Ethereum has:

* vastly more users
* vastly more developers
* vastly more liquidity
* stablecoins
* DeFi
* institutional adoption
* enormous security budget
* huge network effects.

If both become equivalently PQ-secure, users don't automatically migrate to QRL.

Ethereum's present plan attacks quantum vulnerability across all the important layers: ECDSA accounts, BLS consensus signatures, KZG/data commitments and quantum-vulnerable proof systems. Account abstraction is intended to let individual accounts adopt PQ signatures, while leanXMSS/leanVM and other changes address protocol layers. ([ethereum.org][5])

So:

> **“ETH cannot survive quantum, therefore QRL wins”**

is no longer a good thesis.

Ethereum is taking it extremely seriously.

