# But QRL still has one genuinely interesting advantage

### Migration is much harder than greenfield design.

QRL 1.x has been post-quantum from genesis since 2018. ([QRL][8])

Ethereum has to migrate a gigantic live organism:

```text
hundreds of billions in assets
millions of accounts
validators
hardware wallets
custodians
exchanges
bridges
L2s
smart contracts
DeFi
stablecoins
institutional systems
old dormant wallets
```

while continuing to operate.

QRL gets to say:

> **PQ wasn't retrofitted. It is the security model.**

And QRL 2.0 is explicitly building ML-DSA into transactions and validator operations, with crypto-agility and additional PQ algorithms planned. ([QRL][9])

That's meaningful.

Think of the difference as:

### Ethereum

A gigantic aircraft changing engines while flying.

### QRL

An aircraft designed around the new engine.

But the gigantic aircraft has 100,000× more passengers.

Neither advantage automatically wins.

